bash -> // A header whose update-hdr sections cover the shapes a marker line takes, one
bash -> // section per shape.
bash -> // Three sections open one, two and three namespaces on the marker line, and one
bash -> // opens none there because its brace stands on the line below. Five name their
bash -> // namespace in a spelling of its own: the C++17 scope operator, an attribute, an
bash -> // attribute carrying a string argument, an attribute whose own name is qualified,
bash -> // and a comment standing between the keyword and the name.
bash -> // The last five carry text after the name that is not code. A comment spells a call
bash -> // and a semicolon, a line comment mentions another namespace, a line comment ends on
bash -> // the keyword itself, and a quoted and a raw string literal each spell a namespace
bash -> // line of their own. The name each of those lines gives its namespace stands outside
bash -> // that text.
